WEBVTT

0
00:00.340 --> 00:01.810
<v Krista>In this video we're talking about addition</v>

1
00:01.810 --> 00:04.160
and subtraction of signed numbers.

2
00:04.160 --> 00:05.880
And remember that signed numbers

3
00:05.880 --> 00:07.550
are just numbers that have a sign.

4
00:07.550 --> 00:09.910
Either a positive sign or a negative sign.

5
00:09.910 --> 00:12.970
So every number is always going to be a signed number,

6
00:12.970 --> 00:14.740
because it's either going to be a positive number

7
00:14.740 --> 00:15.700
or a negative number.

8
00:15.700 --> 00:18.510
So when we say addition and subtraction of signed numbers,

9
00:18.510 --> 00:19.570
we're just talking about

10
00:19.570 --> 00:21.510
adding two positive numbers together,

11
00:21.510 --> 00:23.490
or adding two negative numbers together,

12
00:23.490 --> 00:26.290
or subtracting a negative number from a positive number,

13
00:26.290 --> 00:28.880
or subtracting a negative number from a negative number.

14
00:28.880 --> 00:31.440
So these are all operations of addition and subtraction

15
00:31.440 --> 00:33.680
that we're doing with signed numbers.

16
00:33.680 --> 00:35.480
So let's take a look at a couple of examples

17
00:35.480 --> 00:38.090
and we're going to plot these on our number line

18
00:38.090 --> 00:40.760
so that we get a better idea of how it works

19
00:40.760 --> 00:43.130
when we add and subtract signed numbers.

20
00:43.130 --> 00:46.180
So, in our first example here we have positive one

21
00:46.180 --> 00:47.490
plus a positive three.

22
00:47.490 --> 00:50.120
We all know that's going to be a positive four.

23
00:50.120 --> 00:52.390
That's simple addition, and the way that we know that

24
00:52.390 --> 00:54.960
if we look at our number line is we always start

25
00:54.960 --> 00:57.870
at the origin, here at zero, and we want to move over

26
00:57.870 --> 00:59.870
one unit because we have a positive one.

27
00:59.870 --> 01:02.510
So, because we move to the right when we have positive

28
01:02.510 --> 01:04.570
and we move to the left when we have a negative number

29
01:04.570 --> 01:06.410
we're going to move to the right one unit.

30
01:06.410 --> 01:08.050
So we're going to move to the right one unit

31
01:08.050 --> 01:09.410
and we're going to be right here.

32
01:09.410 --> 01:11.780
Then because we're adding a positive three,

33
01:11.780 --> 01:14.430
we want to continue moving to the right three more units.

34
01:14.430 --> 01:17.820
So one, two, three more units and you can see

35
01:17.820 --> 01:20.675
that we end up here at four which is why we get a

36
01:20.675 --> 01:23.760
positive four when we add those two numbers together.

37
01:23.760 --> 01:26.110
On the other hand here we're adding together

38
01:26.110 --> 01:27.330
two negative numbers.

39
01:27.330 --> 01:29.140
So here we added two positive numbers

40
01:29.140 --> 01:31.360
and here we're adding two negative numbers.

41
01:31.360 --> 01:32.550
When we have a negative number,

42
01:32.550 --> 01:35.100
it tells us to move to the left on the number line

43
01:35.100 --> 01:37.100
instead of to the right on the number line.

44
01:37.100 --> 01:39.090
So when we have this negative one here,

45
01:39.090 --> 01:42.300
we start at the origin and we move to the left one unit

46
01:42.300 --> 01:43.560
because we have negative one.

47
01:43.560 --> 01:45.510
So we move to the left one unit.

48
01:45.510 --> 01:47.710
Then because we're adding a negative three,

49
01:47.710 --> 01:50.500
we want to continue moving to the left three more units.

50
01:50.500 --> 01:55.500
One, two, three and we get to negative four here.

51
01:55.530 --> 01:58.870
So this is going to be equal to negative four,

52
01:58.870 --> 02:02.470
and the number line shows us that when we take negative one

53
02:02.470 --> 02:03.610
plus a negative three.

54
02:03.610 --> 02:05.950
If on the other hand here we have a positive two

55
02:05.950 --> 02:06.890
plus a negative one,

56
02:06.890 --> 02:09.960
so we have a positive number added to a negative number

57
02:09.960 --> 02:12.420
what we're going to do is start at positive two.

58
02:12.420 --> 02:15.040
That means we start at the origin and we move to the right

59
02:15.040 --> 02:16.860
in the positive direction two units.

60
02:16.860 --> 02:19.520
So we start at the origin we move one,

61
02:19.520 --> 02:22.280
two units to the right in the positive direction.

62
02:22.280 --> 02:24.760
And then we add to that a negative one,

63
02:24.760 --> 02:26.200
which means that we're going to go back

64
02:26.200 --> 02:27.670
to the left one unit.

65
02:27.670 --> 02:31.880
So we go back to the left one unit and we end up right here

66
02:31.880 --> 02:33.290
at positive one.

67
02:33.290 --> 02:37.140
So positive two plus a negative one is going to be equal to

68
02:37.140 --> 02:38.300
a positive one.

69
02:38.300 --> 02:40.420
And these two examples should make sense to us

70
02:40.420 --> 02:42.620
because remember, adding a negative number

71
02:42.620 --> 02:44.230
is just like subtracting.

72
02:44.230 --> 02:46.250
So negative one plus a negative three

73
02:46.250 --> 02:49.650
is the same as negative one minus three.

74
02:49.650 --> 02:51.692
Same thing here, we would have had a positive two

75
02:51.692 --> 02:55.030
plus a negative number, just becomes a minus.

76
02:55.030 --> 02:57.820
So two minus one, both of those are going to give us

77
02:57.820 --> 02:59.580
the same answer here, negative four.

78
02:59.580 --> 03:01.380
And here we get a positive one.

79
03:01.380 --> 03:03.210
So if we look at our next example here,

80
03:03.210 --> 03:06.020
we have a negative three plus a positive two.

81
03:06.020 --> 03:07.820
Adding a positive is still just adding.

82
03:07.820 --> 03:10.730
So this is negative three plus two.

83
03:10.730 --> 03:12.320
Here we're adding a negative number,

84
03:12.320 --> 03:14.150
which we know is the same as subtracting,

85
03:14.150 --> 03:16.510
so we get a minus two.

86
03:16.510 --> 03:18.540
So if we plot this on our number line,

87
03:18.540 --> 03:19.750
we start at the origin and

88
03:19.750 --> 03:21.820
we want to move to the left three units,

89
03:21.820 --> 03:23.340
because we have a negative three.

90
03:23.340 --> 03:27.400
So we say, one, two, three units to negative three.

91
03:27.400 --> 03:28.840
Then we're adding a positive two,

92
03:28.840 --> 03:30.920
we want to go back to the right two units.

93
03:30.920 --> 03:35.050
So one, two, and then we're subtracting a negative number

94
03:35.050 --> 03:36.840
so were just going to the left.

95
03:36.840 --> 03:38.610
This is like adding a negative.

96
03:38.610 --> 03:43.060
We go back to the left one, two and we end up right here

97
03:43.060 --> 03:45.080
at negative three so this is going

98
03:45.080 --> 03:47.430
to be equal to negative three.

99
03:47.430 --> 03:49.340
And of course this should make sense to us because

100
03:49.340 --> 03:52.660
when we add a positive two and then add a negative two

101
03:52.660 --> 03:54.060
that's an inverse operation.

102
03:54.060 --> 03:55.970
We're adding two and we're subtracting two.

103
03:55.970 --> 03:58.590
And you can see when we simplified, we got a plus two

104
03:58.590 --> 04:01.290
and a minus two and those are cancel with each other.

105
04:01.290 --> 04:03.310
A positive two and a negative two,

106
04:03.310 --> 04:05.250
when we add those together we get zero.

107
04:05.250 --> 04:07.550
And a negative three plus zero,

108
04:07.550 --> 04:09.280
negative three plus zero.

109
04:09.280 --> 04:12.450
We know that zero is the identity number for addition,

110
04:12.450 --> 04:15.090
which means that adding zero doesn't change the value

111
04:15.090 --> 04:16.790
of negative three, so of course here

112
04:16.790 --> 04:18.970
we're just going to get negative three.

113
04:18.970 --> 04:21.380
What this tells us is that we can look at subtraction

114
04:21.380 --> 04:22.400
in multiple ways.

115
04:22.400 --> 04:26.040
We said here in this example we had two plus a negative one

116
04:26.040 --> 04:28.280
was the same as two minus one.

117
04:28.280 --> 04:31.730
So this plus a negative, just became two minus one.

118
04:31.730 --> 04:32.950
It became a subtraction.

119
04:32.950 --> 04:36.080
Basically what we're doing is just inserting parenthesis

120
04:36.080 --> 04:37.520
in our mind but we don't write them.

121
04:37.520 --> 04:39.340
So if we look at this example here,

122
04:39.340 --> 04:41.640
we have a negative four minus three.

123
04:41.640 --> 04:44.400
Well that's the same as saying negative four

124
04:44.400 --> 04:47.730
plus a negative three, that's the same thing.

125
04:47.730 --> 04:49.990
So we either have negative four minus three,

126
04:49.990 --> 04:53.010
or we can say negative four plus a negative three.

127
04:53.010 --> 04:55.130
So if it helps you to make everything addition

128
04:55.130 --> 04:57.170
and insert these parenthesis, you can do that.

129
04:57.170 --> 04:59.300
So we have negative four plus a negative three

130
04:59.300 --> 05:02.080
plus two and we can put parenthesis around this also

131
05:02.080 --> 05:03.800
and say plus a positive two.

132
05:03.800 --> 05:06.300
Here we have minus four but we could also say

133
05:06.300 --> 05:11.300
plus a negative four minus three or plus a negative three

134
05:11.360 --> 05:14.510
and minus two or plus a negative two.

135
05:14.510 --> 05:17.430
So now you can see we've connected everything with addition.

136
05:17.430 --> 05:19.060
So it sort of takes away the subtraction

137
05:19.060 --> 05:20.820
and allows us to add everything together.

138
05:20.820 --> 05:23.710
So if we now add all of our negative numbers together.

139
05:23.710 --> 05:26.180
We have a negative four plus a negative three

140
05:26.180 --> 05:28.910
is a negative seven, so that's a negative seven.

141
05:28.910 --> 05:31.220
Plus a negative four is a negative 11.

142
05:31.220 --> 05:34.000
Plus a negative three is a negative 14.

143
05:34.000 --> 05:36.570
Plus a negative two is a negative 16.

144
05:36.570 --> 05:38.740
So adding all of our negative numbers together

145
05:38.740 --> 05:40.300
we get negative 16.

146
05:40.300 --> 05:42.480
The only positive number is this plus two,

147
05:42.480 --> 05:44.980
so we say negative 16 plus two.

148
05:44.980 --> 05:47.050
And if we think about this on our number line

149
05:47.050 --> 05:49.250
negative 16 would have started at the origin

150
05:49.250 --> 05:51.560
and move to the left sixteen units

151
05:51.560 --> 05:54.520
and then the positive two would have us come back two units.

152
05:54.520 --> 05:57.910
So the solution is going to be negative 14.

153
05:57.910 --> 06:00.650
Now the tricky part here is when we get to subtraction

154
06:00.650 --> 06:01.670
of negative numbers.

155
06:01.670 --> 06:03.120
Up until this point we've just done

156
06:03.120 --> 06:04.700
addition of negative numbers,

157
06:04.700 --> 06:06.260
but here we're asking to find

158
06:06.260 --> 06:08.310
negative two minus a negative three.

159
06:08.310 --> 06:10.240
We're subtracting a negative number.

160
06:10.240 --> 06:11.950
And in that case the reason it's tricky

161
06:11.950 --> 06:13.790
is because on our number line we're actually

162
06:13.790 --> 06:15.230
going to move in the opposite direction

163
06:15.230 --> 06:16.480
of the sign that's indicated.

164
06:16.480 --> 06:18.360
So in other words, if we go back and we look at

165
06:18.360 --> 06:21.770
a couple of these first examples we had one plus three

166
06:21.770 --> 06:24.040
this positive sign, this plus sign here,

167
06:24.040 --> 06:25.400
indicates that we're going to go

168
06:25.400 --> 06:28.310
in the direction indicated by this positive three.

169
06:28.310 --> 06:30.120
So because the three is positive we would think

170
06:30.120 --> 06:31.027
that we're going to move to the right

171
06:31.027 --> 06:33.270
and the positive sign tells us yes

172
06:33.270 --> 06:34.480
you are going to move to the right.

173
06:34.480 --> 06:36.620
Here, we had a negative three

174
06:36.620 --> 06:37.960
and this positive sign tells us

175
06:37.960 --> 06:39.080
we're going to move in the direction

176
06:39.080 --> 06:41.190
that is indicated by the negative three.

177
06:41.190 --> 06:42.310
By the number that follows it.

178
06:42.310 --> 06:43.900
So negative three tells us we're going to move

179
06:43.900 --> 06:46.610
to the left and the positive sign says yes,

180
06:46.610 --> 06:47.810
you're going to move to the left.

181
06:47.810 --> 06:50.660
When we have a subtraction sign on the other hand

182
06:50.660 --> 06:52.950
we're going to move in the opposite direction indicated.

183
06:52.950 --> 06:55.120
So this negative three right here tells us,

184
06:55.120 --> 06:57.260
we're going to move to the left, because it's negative.

185
06:57.260 --> 06:58.760
But the subtraction sign says

186
06:58.760 --> 07:00.510
you're going to flip that operation,

187
07:00.510 --> 07:01.970
you're not going to move to the left,

188
07:01.970 --> 07:03.930
you're going to move to the right instead.

189
07:03.930 --> 07:06.160
So what this looks like is we're going to start

190
07:06.160 --> 07:08.630
at negative two, we're going to start at the origin

191
07:08.630 --> 07:10.560
and we're going to move to the left two units

192
07:10.560 --> 07:12.020
because we start with this negative two.

193
07:12.020 --> 07:15.200
So one, two, and we get to negative two right here.

194
07:15.200 --> 07:18.030
Then normally if we were adding negative three

195
07:18.030 --> 07:20.480
we would continue moving to the left three units,

196
07:20.480 --> 07:22.570
but because we're subtracting negative three,

197
07:22.570 --> 07:25.620
instead of moving to the left, we'll move back to the right

198
07:25.620 --> 07:28.420
three units, so one, two, three.

199
07:28.420 --> 07:31.870
And that's going to get us right here to positive one.

200
07:31.870 --> 07:34.820
So this is going to be equal to positive one.

201
07:34.820 --> 07:36.860
Another way to remember that is that when you have

202
07:36.860 --> 07:38.990
negative signs back to back like this,

203
07:38.990 --> 07:40.840
when we're subtracting a negative sign.

204
07:40.840 --> 07:43.070
Two negative signs back to back like this

205
07:43.070 --> 07:45.200
will cancel with each other and become a positive.

206
07:45.200 --> 07:47.560
You can cancel every two negative signs.

207
07:47.560 --> 07:49.990
So we have to pair them up and then we can cancel them.

208
07:49.990 --> 07:53.030
You can't cancel three negative signs that are back to back

209
07:53.030 --> 07:54.170
just two at a time.

210
07:54.170 --> 07:56.120
So because we have exactly two here,

211
07:56.120 --> 07:58.760
we can cancel them out and they become a positive.

212
07:58.760 --> 08:02.010
So essentially negative two minus a negative three

213
08:02.010 --> 08:05.130
becomes negative two plus a positive three

214
08:05.130 --> 08:07.250
or just negative two plus three.

215
08:07.250 --> 08:09.110
And then in that case of course, we can see,

216
08:09.110 --> 08:10.670
that we start at the origin

217
08:10.670 --> 08:13.640
and we move two units to the left to negative two.

218
08:13.640 --> 08:16.430
And then we move three units to the right, positive three.

219
08:16.430 --> 08:19.860
One, two, three and we get back to the same place

220
08:19.860 --> 08:22.580
that we landed when we subtracted a negative three.

221
08:22.580 --> 08:25.040
So it's the same thing, we've just simplified by

222
08:25.040 --> 08:26.833
removing that double negative.